{"name":"Cranberry Pie","hex":"#c27277","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cranberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub belonging to the section Vaccinium sect. Oxycoccus of the genus Vaccinium.","The edible red berry of that shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the intense red colour of a cranberry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cranberry"},{"term":"pie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Piro."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pastry that consists of an outer crust and a filling. (Savory pies are more popular in the UK and sweet pies are more popular in the US, so \"pie\" without qualification has different connotations in these dialects.)","Any of various other, non-pastry dishes that maintain the general concept of a shell with a filling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cranberry","blocks":[{"text":"Cranberries are a group of evergreen dwarf shrubs or trailing vines in the subgenus Oxycoccus of the genus Vaccinium. Cranberries are low, creeping shrubs or vines up to 2 meters (7 ft) long and 5 to 20 centimeters in height; they have slender stems that are not thickly woody and have small evergreen leaves. The flowers are dark pink. The fruit is a berry that is larger than the leaves of the plant; it is initially light green, turning red when ripe. The raw berry is edible and has a tart taste due to the low sugar content and high acidity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cranberry_bog.jpg/330px-Cranberry_bog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranberry","wikidata":"Q13181"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cranberries20101210.jpg/500px-Cranberries20101210.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cranberries20101210.jpg/500px-Cranberries20101210.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Raw cranberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACranberries20101210.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg/500px-Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg/500px-Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cranberry harvest","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/%D0%96%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%96%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/%D0%96%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg/1280px-%D0%96%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B0%